# feature-nilpy-starred-and-nested-unpacking — a NESTED loop target.
#
# Reported `expected a second loop variable` before, which claims a variable is
# MISSING while the user is looking straight at one — it is simply parenthesised.
# The for-target is a flat name list and the whole lowering is keyed on it, so
# the gap is real; only the message is fixed here.
nested = [(1, ("a", "b"))]
for n, (p, q) in nested:
    print(n, p, q)
